<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements. Required for notarization: Apple refuses to
  notarize an app that is not signed with the hardened runtime, and the
  hardened runtime blocks things Electron cannot work without unless they are
  requested here.

  Each of these is the minimum Electron needs, and nothing more:

  - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      V8 compiles JavaScript to machine code at runtime. Without both, the
      renderer crashes on launch.
  - disable-library-validation
      The encrypted SQLite driver (better-sqlite3-multiple-ciphers) is a native
      .node module signed with OUR certificate, not Apple's. Library validation
      would refuse to load it, and the app cannot open its database at all.

  Deliberately ABSENT:

  - com.apple.security.app-sandbox
      This is a Developer ID build distributed directly, not a Mac App Store
      build. The sandbox would break the practitioner choosing where her
      encrypted backups are written, which is the one thing she must always be
      able to do.
  - Any network, camera, microphone or contacts entitlement
      The app asks for no OS permissions; Electron's permission handler is
      default-deny (threat model T-09).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
